id: pm-0574of
title: "The history merge driver dedups records by ts, author, op, patch and message only, so a merge silently drops the other copy's compaction receipt, event_class or reanchor_evidence and later readers see rewritten work as original"
description: "The history merge driver dedups records across branches by an identity of ts, author, op, patch and message, and keeps the ours copy. The identity leaves out context, event_class and reanchor_evidence, so two records that agree on those five fields but differ in provenance collapse into one. The surviving copy then silently loses the other copy's compaction receipt, declared event class or rewrite evidence. Readers that rely on that provenance, such as the stale-claim takeover's rewrite detection and compaction receipts, then see a record that looks original. Codex found two reproductions while reviewing the stale-takeover redesign."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: claims,history,merge,provenance
created_at: "2026-11-15T23:42:37.655Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T23:42:37.655Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "historyEntryIdentity covers provenance fields, or a provenance mismatch on an identity match is refused or kept deterministically; Regressions cover the equal-checkpoint baseline receipt case and the rebased-update event_class and reanchor_evidence case; A stale-claim takeover regression proves a merge cannot turn rewritten_history into a permitted takeover"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Merging two records that agree on ts, author, op, patch and message but differ in provenance keeps both provenances or refuses, never silently drops one"
actual_result: "The merge keeps the ours copy and discards the theirs copy's context, event_class and reanchor_evidence"
