  pm-gh1336,discovered_from,"2026-11-15T23:42:37.655Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
body: "## Observed\n\n`historyEntryIdentity` in `src/sdk/merge/three-way.ts` is:\n\n```ts\nstableStringify({ ts, author, op, patch, message })\n```\n\n`mergeHistoryStreams` treats records with equal identity as the same record and keeps ours.\n\nReproductions (Codex, production history builders, both merged chains verify):\n\n1. Two branches compact different prefixes into the same snapshot with equal checkpoint timestamps, authors and entry counts. Their baselines share an identity but carry different receipts, and the merge keeps ours.\n2. After a July 1 claim, merging title updates reduces a substantive July 3 title-plus-order update to the same patch as an independent July 3 order-only update. A second merge keeps the maintenance copy and drops the other copy's `event_class` and `reanchor_evidence`.\n\nIn both cases the stale-claim takeover then treats rewritten or uncertain work as original (scenario 2: `rewritten_history` with 48 idle hours becomes a permitted takeover at 72).\n\n## Fix direction\n\n- Include the provenance fields (`context`, `event_class`, `reanchor_evidence`, `record_hash`) in the dedup identity. Alternatively, treat a match on the five fields with different provenance as a conflict that refuses, or that keeps both records in a deterministic order, instead of silently keeping ours.\n- Add regressions for both scenarios at the `mergeHistoryStreams` level, plus one through the stale-claim takeover."
